  "next_id": 46,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -9,
        -34
      ],
      "id": 45,
      "text": "Field-oriented control (FOC) of a PMSM motor (4 pole pairs, 12 V, 3000 rpm) with Hall sensors on a Blue Pill (firmware/bldc_foc, fixed point, 10 kHz).\nEach PWM period: phase currents from the bridge's current-sense outputs SO1, SO2 (1.65 V + 0.2 V/A) on PA6, PA7; the angle from the Hall sectors;\nClarke and Park transforms; PI controllers hold id at 0 and iq at the setpoint; inverse transforms and space-vector duties on IN1-IN3.\nRV1 sets the torque current (0-2 A, 40 % = 0.8 A); drag M1 for its load. Analyzer > UART: \"RPM <n> IQ* <mA> IQ <mA> ID <mA>\".\nExperimental parts (E-11): about real time with the default settings."
    }
  ],
